[2026-11-24T22:14:15Z] note: assumptions: (1) 100% of equity per trade instead of the spec's risk_fraction sizing (user's library-wide choice, see absolute_momentum_monthly); risk_fraction not in SPACE. (2) Costs = library convention (user-approved): ETF/stock 0.05%+0.03%, above the spec's 5 bp. (3) Fills on adjusted prices: no separate raw series in the project. (4) Spec Min/Max used as ranges; steps chosen for ~10-25 values per parameter; hard_min/hard_max keep levels meaningful. (5) Non-US listings excluded from screening (other currency and costs). (6) Work split: research-library SHARD3, coordinated with the parallel library sessions; first pass = base 0.5 h, screen, broad basket 1 h.
[2026-11-24T22:14:15Z] note: backtest.py adapted from template: strategy block = spec indicators per INDICATORS.md (Wilder RMA and EMA seeded with the SMA of the first n values, population std, flat denominators per spec) with a per-frame LRU cache. Machinery changed: _simulate replaced by the library ATR-exit engine (stop/target = entry fill -/+ k x Wilder ATR(14) of the signal bar, frozen; target fills at its level, stop at the open on a gap; stop before target in one bar; time exit after max_candles completed held bars; entry skipped if ATR<=0 or stop<=0; one fully flat bar after an intrabar exit before a new signal), and run() vetoes an entry when the signal exit is already true on the signal bar. Reason: EXECUTION.md exits depend on the entry and can't be plain sell signals.
